  "description": "Matt has been basically riding non-stop since we sat him down on his very own signature frame dubbed the MR1. Although Matt’s big burly riding style hasn’t changed, he wanted to fine-tune a few things on his frame and change the theme to freshen it up a bit. We added to the standover height and changed it from 8.75_ to 9_ to make the bike a little more stable. The B.B. was also raised just a little bit, for a little extra pop. We also increased the length of the dropout slot to make the frame compatible with more gear ratios, and it also makes it easier to remove the rear wheel during repairs. Matt Ray Signature Frame Sizes: 20.5_, 20.75_, 21_, 21.2_ 4130 chromoly, double butted top tube and down tube Head tube: 75° / 120mm Seat tube: 71° / 9.0_ / integrated seat clamp Chainstay Length: 13.3_ – 14_ BB: 11.5_/ 38mm – Mid Weight: 4.8 lbs (20.5_) Colors: Black, Matte Trans Orange **Please note that transparent and translucent paints may reveal surface oxidation on chromoly / steel components. It is important to understand that this oxidation does not impact the structural strength of the part, and is not deemed as a defect. Nevertheless, if you prefer to avoid surface oxidation, we recommend selecting a solid-colored option.",
